# Styling — Tailwind + design tokens

This project uses **Tailwind CSS** with a custom **"Bold & Playful Paper"**
theme: warm paper surfaces, heavy ink borders, offset shadows, four accents.

## Design tokens

- **Colors are CSS custom properties** defined in `src/styles/global.css`, as
  RGB channels (`--bg-rgb: 247 244 236`) so Tailwind opacity modifiers work
  (`text-ink/60`, `bg-bg/85`).
- **Semantic colors only.** Use `bg`, `ink`, `panel`, `card`, and `a1`–`a4`
  wired through `tailwind.config.js`. Never hard-code hex/rgb values in
  components or className strings.
- **Light + dark** share the same accents; dark mode is the `.dark` class on
  `<html>`, toggled by `ThemeContext`. New tokens must be defined for both.

## Reusable component classes

Defined in `global.css`; prefer these over re-deriving utility soup:
`.card` / `.card--shadow`, `.btn` / `.btn--ghost`, `.chip` / `.chip--btn` /
`.chip--active`, `.lift`, `.nav-link` / `.nav-link--active`, `.font-display` /
`.kicker`, `.shape` / `.fill-a1`–`.fill-a4`, `.paper-grid`, `.rise`.

## Layout conventions

- Section wrapper: `max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-20`
- Section kicker/label: `kicker text-ink/60 mb-3`
- Section heading: `font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl`
- Project/listing grids are responsive 1 → 2 → 3 columns.

## Rules

- **Tokens before new values.** Adding a color or shadow means adding a CSS
  variable + a Tailwind mapping, not inlining a literal.
- **Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`** for entrance animations (`.rise`,
  `.lift`).
- **Keep `tailwind.config.js` and `global.css` in sync** — every semantic color
  in the config must resolve to a defined CSS variable.
- Global styles are imported once via `gatsby-browser.js`
  (`import "./src/styles/global.css"`); don't import CSS into individual
  components.
